# Inert PMO scalar subject reader opt-in
Based on062ac21; Finance files/checkpoint unchanged. Keyword-only closed boolean `_reader_scalar=False` added only to subject, issue_subject, read_scope, observation, selected_access, legacy_access. Default full subject queryset and native errors retained. True adds only(pk,case_id,kind); exact samecase/kind/agent-private/public-evidence checks remain. Flag propagates explicitly through this reader chain, never acts as permission. No global/ContextVar mode or caller-controlled fields/queryset.
No binding_access/report_source_access/template caller wiring. No other projections, baseline_manifest changes, preflight integration, routes or DB work. Legacy state existence lookup remains unconditional. Existing defaults retain their eager bodies; opted-in subject result is deferred and trusted future reader must not access body. This is NOT complete leadership/incident bounded admission.
Five isolated pure tests pass normal/-O: default/scalar queryshape, unchanged evidence errors/closedbool, public gate, exact keyword propagation and unconditional legacy state query/no activation. Native SQL equivalence and fixtures UNRUN. Current modern/legacy constructor design remains separate, full report dependency not cleared by this patch.
